Platform: Core Ultra 7 155H (Meteor Lake-H): 6 P-cores with SMT, 8 E-cores in two
4-core clusters on the compute tile, 2 LP E-cores on the SoC tile. CPU topology
only; the Meteor Lake iGPU and NPU ids are covered by the platform tables and
other fixtures.

Sources (kernel paths are Linux v6.18 (torvalds/linux tag v6.18)):
- 6 P + 8 E + 2 LP E, 22 threads: Intel ark, Core Ultra 7 155H (product 236847),
  as listed in Wikipedia "Meteor Lake", Meteor Lake-H table.
- cpu_core/cpu_atom: MTL is hybrid_big_small in arch/x86/events/intel/core.c, so
  its LP E-cores (the same Crestmont core as the E-cores) are listed in cpu_atom;
  tools/perf/Documentation/intel-hybrid.txt for the files.
- cache/index*/level and shared_cpu_list, topology/core_cpus_list:
  Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-devices-system-cpu.
- The LP E-cores have no L3: Wikipedia "Meteor Lake", SoC tile, citing Chips and
  Cheese "Comparing Crestmonts: No L3 Hurts" (2024-05-20).

Not from hardware: the CPU numbering (P threads 0-11 as sibling pairs, E 12-19,
LP E 20-21), the cache index numbering, the kernel release string and the
cpuinfo flags line. No acpi_cppc files, so no favored CPUs are reported.
